window.docContents[64].resolve({"/Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels/#Statlib--Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels":{"contents":"Statistical decision theory gives a mathematical language for discussing\noptimality and accuracy in statistical methods. Informally, the workflow has\nfour stages:\n\n1. run an experiment to study an object of interest;2. use the observation from the experiment to choose an action or decision;3. quantify the precision of that action;4. search for the best decision rule for the workflow.\n\nBecause the process moves from one measurable object to the next, a natural\ngeneral framework is that of Markov kernels.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Statlib","header":"2. Statistical Risk and Markov Kernels","id":"/Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels/#Statlib--Statistical-Risk-and-Markov-Kernels"}});